# Gollum, Riddle Master: "choose one that hasn't been chosen". A modal triggered ability's mode is chosen as it is put on
# the stack (CR 603.3c, 700.2), so a mode chosen for a trigger that is then countered has still been chosen. Gollum (even)
# sees Bot2's Mox Jet (mana value 0) cast: Bot1 chooses the +1/+1 counter at once. In response Bot2 flashes in Ertai
# Resurrected (mana value 4, even), which triggers Gollum again: the counter mode is spent - refused - and Bot1 chooses to
# draw. That trigger resolves (Bot1 draws). Ertai enters and counters the first trigger (Bot1, its controller, draws). So
# Gollum never gets the counter, Bot1 drew two cards, and the modes chosen are the counter and the draw - the counter
# chosen though its ability never resolved.

